lines=['# Policy ablation: validation and frozen design','','All rates here are exploratory validation results. The 128-ID prescreen is a prefix of the 512-ID validation set, not an additional independent corpus. The final test choices were locked before opening any new confirmatory outcomes.','','## Implemented policies','','The C++ path retains partitioned initialization, conditional repair with fixed exterior, exact syndrome checks and observable-frame construction. A model-only preparation computes at most 128 independently parity-checked kernel moves per band. Bounded beam search uses depth at most two and K in {1,2,4,8,16}. It preserves low-cost configurations and some distinct full logical signatures; this is a heuristic search with no completeness claim. At most two conditional solver calls are allowed per decode, in addition to initialization/fallback. Every primary workload has one B4 seam. Radius two is the whole non-invisible region; a third or independent combined region would duplicate it and was not fabricated.','','Policy A (`cost`) includes the incumbent, deduplicates configurations, and accepts only a strictly lower configuration cost (tolerance 1e-10). Every kernel perturbation preserves D_J z=t_J; final full syndrome/frame gates are retained. Policy B (`class_mass`) sums exp(-C) over unique retained configurations within each logical signature and selects the cheapest representative in the winning class. It can increase configuration cost, is a separately named policy, and has no original monotone-cost theorem. Its biased, bounded candidate pool has no exact posterior/MAP interpretation, no exhaustive class coverage, and no claim of calibrated relative class mass.','','Adaptive radius1→radius2 uses only BP nonconvergence, fewer than two retained logical signatures, a configuration gap below 0.5, or an empty first band. These are fixed decoder-visible triggers. The ensemble makes a second bounded BP proposal with an alternative scale only when nonconverged or logically redundant; true observables never generate candidates or trigger escalation. The serial BP schedule is the official variable-serial LDPC schedule, not check-layered BP. No graph, fault prior, shared physical fault, or observable mapping was changed.','','## Fixed-budget prescreen (128 validation IDs)','','| Workload | Variant | Failures | Mean ms | p99 ms |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|']
allpoints=[]
